{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/deviant-the-renegades/1448449-deviant-inspirations-for-conspiracies-from-anime-manga","id":1448449,"title":"Deviant Inspirations for Conspiracies from Anime/Manga","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Deviant: The Renegades"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-13T12:15:37-07:00","id":1448449,"title":"Deviant Inspirations for Conspiracies from Anime/Manga","content":"So for the Anime/Manga crowd there are some really good examples of organizations that would turn people into things that hit from the top of my head. I won't be giving any spoilers that weren't mentioned in the Kickstarter video or are general public knowledge, but here we go. These are two that I thought of while reading the backer copy that give excellent sources for inspiration.<br /> <br /> <br /> Bio-Booster Armor Guyver - Kronos Corporation - The Manga practically reads like it could be a Deviant chronicle that has some mere humans along for the ride. Everyone from our Main character Sho, on down is touch and scared by the Shadowy international group that manufactures superhuman, loyal monsters (call Zoanoids) for their own sinister plans. This would be a good example of a high rated super powerful conspiracy. By the second half it would be what happens if the other guys win as they end up running the world and get people to line up for processing into Zoanoids and everyone just accepts it by the second half. Sadly only the first half of the manga was ever officially translated into English. The redo of the Anime also follows the Source better than the 80's/90's adaptation but still cuts out early but does start to enter the second half.<br /> <br /> Killing Bites - Killing Bites Tournament - You can watch this on Amazon Prime Video, the first half reads like a . Serval Mega Corps have annual artificial therianthrope brawls to determine power structure amongst themselves, while the Corps involved would be mid rank conspiracies' as they are the 4 most powerful corporations in Japan rather than international outfits with offices around the world like above, the organization that puts this on for them, would be a much smaller conspiracy with only a few key players. So this one again could provide a lot of inspiration for characters and even hints that you can use myths about animals as a source for powers. Like Porcupines shooting quills (like arrows).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-27T02:42:32-07:00","id":1521456,"title":"","content":"Brynhildr in the Darknes - A research institute (the conspiracy) is running secret and shady experiments on kidnapped girls. The experiments grant a variety of ESP powers (variations) to the so-called &quot;witches&quot;. However, the power comes at cost of terrible and life-threatening side effects (scars). Someday, Neko Kuroha a &quot;witch&quot; with no memories of her past life, and some of her friends, manage to flee from the institute and then helped by a boy with the gift of eidetic memory, the runaway &quot;witches&quot; will engage an unequal and desperate battle against the research institute's evil schemes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 09-02-2023, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T11:03:50-07:00","id":1521823,"title":"","content":"The folks who made Mad Pierrot from Cowboy Bebop would be a good inspo. They experimented to turn this guy into a terrifying super-soldier (Variations), but in the process he regressed mentally into childhood (scar).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T15:19:30-07:00","id":1521840,"title":"","content":"From the To aru franchise ( To Aru Majutsu no Index, To Aru Kagaku no Railgun, etc.) you got a full web of pain of organizations here are a pair of links if you want a list of organizations for <a href=\"https://toarumajutsunoindex.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Magic_Side_Factions_and_Organizations\" target=\"_blank\">The Magic Side</a> and another for the <a href=\"https://toarumajutsunoindex.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Science_Side_Factions_and_Organizations\" target=\"_blank\">The Science Side</a> you can take your pick for renegades and devoted among them too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth",